{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["According to its entirety: 'is praised' — two joined as one. And likewise the interpretation: 'For his mouth's sake' — because he multiplies understanding, people praise him. But one of twisted heart they despise, and he is despised and abased. In his eyes and his understanding, 'a servant who acquires for himself' is better than one honored who had abundant wealth but lost it through his folly, and afterward lacked bread. And 'honored' is the opposite of 'despised,' meaning he is honored in his own eyes yet lacks bread — good is the despised one [by contrast]."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The comment is textually difficult: the citation בעבור פיהו does not match Prov. 12:8 (לפי שכלו ישבחוהו); it may reflect a variant reading or a conflation. The final clause טוב הנקלה is rendered hyper-literally; the syntax is compressed and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:21.525650049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}